  "response_text": "While you can use printf, a debugger is faster and doesn\u2019t require a recompile each time you want to observe a different value. It may also be more reliable since calling printf may cause values to change/be inaccurate. In addition, it may be hard to know exactly where register values are during runtime if you were to use printf, thus making the debugger an easier choice. Also, a debugger is specifically for debugging and viewing registers, not printf.\\n",
